From c06470d4c05c5811efbd9884c1004415f2fc5fa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:15:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 123/210] media: amlogic: amvdec: add VP9 decoding

Decode VP9 frame requests on GXL, GXM, G12A, G12B and SM1 through
VDEC_HEVC. GX uses gxl_vp9.bin and non-MMU reference surfaces.
Use request snapshots for frame parameters and timestamp references,
with shared compressed capture backing and per-picture MV bounds.

Support profiles 0 and 2, including dimensions down to 16 pixels.
GX converts 10-bit input to 8-bit NV12M output through double-write.
Retain reference metadata until buffer reuse is safe, complete hidden
frames through the request API and restart the stream counter at a key
frame while preserving request ownership.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5 Claude:claude-fable-5.1 Codex:gpt-5.6 Codex:gpt-6.0
[chewitt: give the VP9 frame control a valid 8x8 default, sort and
 tidy the per-SoC format tables, limit GXBB HEVC to 1080p, decode
 H.264 up to 4K on GXL and GXM, and accept HEVC coded sizes up to
 4096x2304]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
